WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.897
Decoder-only generation is easy to see with a small model such as DistilGPT2.

00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:11.787
The text-generation pipeline receives a prompt and repeatedly predicts additional tokens.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:15.967
max_new_tokens limits how many new tokens can be generated.

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:22.202
do_sample set to True means the model samples from the probability distribution instead of always choosing the

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:26.257
single highest-probability token.

00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:33.617
temperature changes how concentrated that distribution is; lower values usually make output more predictable,

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.537
while higher values allow more variation.

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:40.662
Run the example several times and compare the continuations.

00:00:40.662 --> 00:00:45.517
Because sampling is involved, the text can change from run to run.

00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:53.347
DistilGPT2 is useful for teaching the mechanics of generation, but it is an older, small completion model,

00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:56.247
not a modern instruction-following assistant.

00:00:56.247 --> 00:01:02.135
The goal is to observe autoregressive decoding, not to evaluate current chat-model quality.
